[
    {
        "content": "<p>Lately, I've been working with some intricate algebraic constructions and I keep running into the same problem: having to prove by hand a bunch of <code>IsScalarTower</code> instances. For example, here is piece of a PR I'm currently working on:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n<span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower.to₁₃₄</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span>\n<span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower.to₁₂₄</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span>\n<span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower.to₁₂₄</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C₀</span>\n<span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower.to₁₂₄</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span>\n<span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower.to₁₃₄</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span>\n<span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower.to₁₃₄</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span>\n<span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower.to₁₂₄</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- ... (10 more lines of the same flavour)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>As one can see, all of these follow the same pattern: try to apply <code>to₁₂₃</code>, <code>to₁₂₄</code>, <code>to₁₃₄</code>, and <code>of_algebraMap_eq'</code> until you get what you want. Of course, some clever thinking can speed up the process by figuring out the right pathway but it usually just faster, at least for me <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span>,  to mechanically try out different things until it works </p>\n<p>So I was thinking: what if there was a tactic that, given a goal <code>IsScalarTower A B C</code> generates automatically  a proof for it? The rough idea would be to enumerate the types in the local context, apply those four lemmas to generate new instances and subgoals, recurse, and in the end prune the results to keep only what's needed.</p>\n<p>Before I go down this rabbit hole, I'd love to hear what people think:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Is this a good idea / does it seem useful?</li>\n<li>Is there already something that could help with the process and that I missed?</li>\n<li>Is there a smarter way to go about it?</li>\n<li>Is this a reasonable project to take on?</li>\n</ul>\n<p>I should mention that I know absolutely nothing about tactic programming, but I'm willing to give it a shot with the help of my new friend Claude.</p>",
        "id": 576960756,
        "sender_full_name": "Xavier Roblot",
        "timestamp": 1772540217
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>you could write a macro that expands to a call to <code>solve_by_elim</code></p>",
        "id": 576962260,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1772540722
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sounds like a good idea. Let me see if I can understand how it works</p>",
        "id": 576989363,
        "sender_full_name": "Xavier Roblot",
        "timestamp": 1772547903
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi Xavier,</p>\n<p>I've had something a little bit similar before, where I had to provide a bunch of proofs of IsScalarTower for the following diagram (going up is an algebra inclusion)</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">                             </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                           </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"bp\">\\</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                          </span><span class=\"n\">D</span><span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"n\">E</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                        </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">\\</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                       </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"n\">C</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                        </span><span class=\"bp\">\\</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                          </span><span class=\"n\">A</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>but in the end - I managed to fix it by declaring a bunch of instances which \"fill in\" the missing <code>IsScalarTower</code> automatically. I'm sure you had a look at this as well but is there a reason this this did not work for you?</p>",
        "id": 576999510,
        "sender_full_name": "Xavier Généreux",
        "timestamp": 1772550316
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In my case, the algebras are built by composing ring homomorphisms via <code>RingHom.toAlgebra</code>, so  the <code>IsScalarTower</code> instances depend on the specific ring homomorphisms and have to be proved on the fly and that's what I'd like the tactic to do!</p>",
        "id": 577002878,
        "sender_full_name": "Xavier Roblot",
        "timestamp": 1772551129
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Why not post a (possibly not minimal) working example so we can see what's happening? One might imagine that typeclass inference could do this by itself, I think that would be the naive hope, and it would be interesting to see how it is failing.</p>",
        "id": 577009514,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1772552486
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My understanding is that: Assuming <code>Algebra A B</code> <code>Algebra B C</code> and then <em>defining</em> <code>Algebra A C</code> and <code>IsScalarTower A B C</code> from their composition is equivalent to simply assuming <code>Algebra A B</code> <code>Algebra B C</code> <code>Algebra A C</code> <code>IsScalarTower A B C</code> - just more annoying to work with and generally should be avoided.</p>",
        "id": 577017870,
        "sender_full_name": "Xavier Généreux",
        "timestamp": 1772554410
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But yeah, an as Kevin mentioned, an example would be great, maybe this is not what you mean.</p>",
        "id": 577018322,
        "sender_full_name": "Xavier Généreux",
        "timestamp": 1772554511
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ok. I tried to cook up a simplified example. Say I have a field extension <code>L/K</code>, <code>F : IntermediateField K L</code>, a subring <code>A</code> of  <code>K</code>, a subring<code>B</code> of <code>F</code>  such that <code>IsScalarTower A K F</code> and  <code>IsScalarTower A B F</code> holds. </p>\n<p>Now, for the proof, I need to embed <code>F</code> into a larger extension <code>M/L/K</code> -- that's because I need the top field to be Galois to reduce to an already proved special case--, so that gives me a new field <code>F' : IntermediateField K M</code> and now I need to prove <code>IsScalarTower A K F'</code> and <code>IsScalarTower A B F'</code>. So I get something like that:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">FieldTheory</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IntermediateField</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IntermediateField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IntermediateField</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">extendTop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IntermediateField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">algHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IntermediateField</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">extendTopMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→+*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">extendTop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">equivMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">algHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">extendTop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">extendTopMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toAlgebra</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">algebraMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">algebraMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toAlgebra</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">of_algebraMap_eq'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">algebraMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">algebraMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toAlgebra</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">of_algebraMap_eq'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">of_algebraMap_eq'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">to₁₂₃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">to₁₃₄</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F'</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsScalarTower</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">to₁₂₄</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F'</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Note that, to prove <code>IsScalarTower A B F'</code>, I did what I think the tactic should do: I tried to apply combinations of  <code> IsScalarTower.to₁₂₃</code>,<code>IsScalarTower.to₁₂₄</code>,  <code>IsScalarTower.to₁₃₄</code> and <code>IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' rfl</code> until it works <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span></p>",
        "id": 577026333,
        "sender_full_name": "Xavier Roblot",
        "timestamp": 1772556377
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I haven't has time to take a closer look but if the proofs are always like this you could maybe do a macro that tries <code>grind</code> with <code>IsScalarTower.to₁₂₃ IsScalarTower.to₁₃₄ IsScalarTower.to₁₂₄</code> and <code>solve_by_elim/aesop</code> with <code>IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq'</code>.</p>",
        "id": 577072863,
        "sender_full_name": "Xavier Généreux",
        "timestamp": 1772572071
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>i wonder if some <code>algebraize</code> invocation will close this goal?</p>",
